GUI modernization: closing a real gap in Phase 4, found by checking the
phase's own gate against the live app rather than trusting the earlier
"Phase 4 is now fully closed" progress-log entry at face value.

## 1. What was actually wrong

Phase 4's gate (execution order §9) reads: "Implement §4.5 (localization
contract, kind catalogue, structured errors) and §4.6 (formatting
service). Apply the full §5 content contract." ADR 0004 covers §4.5 only
- its Decision section never mentions §5 or §4.6 - and its own "Phase 4
is closed" status line is accurate about ITS OWN scope. The progress
log's separate claim, "Phase 4 is now fully closed" (its own words,
dated during the structured-error-codes slice), was not: it substantiated
that sentence with only ADR 0004's item list, silently treating "every
item this ADR named" as equivalent to "the whole phase gate," which it
was not.

Checked directly against the live dictionary rather than assumed:
- `nav_overview` still read "الصحة", `rules_title` still read "قواعد
  الارتباط", `severity_error` still read "خطأ", and 48 other keys named
  in the execution order's §5.2 direct-replacement table were still their
  pre-review text - the table had never been applied.
- "الراصد" (the glossary's own "avoid in every instance" term) appeared
  in 18 places; "جامعات" (also blanket-avoid) in 1. Neither swept.
- The three §5.3 wizard corrections (language-step title, privacy-step
  title, permissions-step title) were unapplied, and the "a live version
  would have checked..." conditional card - explicitly named for removal
  - was still rendering unconditionally in the Permissions step, above
  the already-honest "skipped, no live recorder" card beneath it.
- No shared formatting module existed anywhere in `desktop/src`. Ten
  call sites across eight files independently repeated
  `date.toLocaleTimeString(lang === "ar" ? "ar-EG" : "en-US", {hour12:
  false})`. A live screenshot taken earlier this session (Rules-page
  work, unrelated task) had already shown the actual consequence without
  it being connected to Phase 4 at the time: incident/event timestamps
  rendered as Arabic-Indic digits ("٢٢:٢٠:٢٢") while every other number
  on the same screen (confidence, counts, IDs) used Latin digits via
  `TechnicalValue`/`ltr-field` - a real, visible inconsistency, not a
  theoretical one.

## 2. What was built

**§5 content contract** - applied via a small Node script (76 exact,
asserted-unique string replacements; two more caught by a follow-up grep
sweep after the first pass) rather than manual editing, so every
substitution is a recorded, auditable line rather than an unlogged hand
edit:
- The full §5.2 direct-replacement table, verbatim, with one deliberate
  adaptation recorded rather than silently applied as-is:
  `settings_refresh_label`'s table text ("تحديث البيانات كل") drops the
  "(seconds)" unit that the original label supplied right before a bare
  `<input type="number">` with nothing after it - kept as "تحديث البيانات
  كل (بالثواني)" so the field does not lose its only unit indicator.
- The three §5.3 wizard title corrections, the "جامعات" -> "وحدات جمع
  البيانات" correction (extended to the three-state string the code
  actually has, not just the two-state example given), and the sample-step
  retitle.
- The "would check" card removed from `PermissionsStep.tsx` entirely
  (component change, not just a string edit) - demo mode now shows only
  the pre-existing, already-honest "Skipped - no live recording service
  to check" card, with nothing above it describing a hypothetical check
  that never runs.
- The privacy paragraph split from one long `<p>` into five `<li>` points
  (`wizard_privacy_point_recorded/_not_recorded/_storage/_device/_bundle`,
  both languages) - same facts as before (cross-checked against
  `docs/product/data-policy.md`, which the component's own comment cites
  as its source), restructured for a reader who skims, not walled by one
  paragraph.
- A full sweep for the glossary's blanket-avoid terms ("الراصد", "حي" as
  a live/direct descriptor, "متوقف" for a down status, "نقطة الاتصال"
  unqualified) beyond the §5.2 table's named keys, since §5.1 states
  these as avoid-everywhere rules, not table-scoped ones. Every fix
  re-checked for Arabic gender agreement where "الراصد" (masculine) became
  "خدمة التسجيل" (feminine) - e.g. `evidence_export_note`'s "واجهته" ->
  "واجهتها", `capabilities_in_bundle`'s "الذي أنتج" -> "التي أنتجت".

**§4.6 formatting service** - `desktop/src/i18n/format.ts` (new):
`formatTime`/`formatDateTime` (both locales now `ar-EG-u-nu-latn`
in Arabic, forcing Latin numerals instead of the default Arabic-Indic
ones - the actual fix for the screenshot-confirmed defect),
`formatCount` (thousands grouping), `formatDuration` (compact «4 س 49 د»
/ detailed «4 ساعات و49 دقيقة», both styles matching the execution
order's own literal examples exactly, checked with an equality
assertion, not a substring match). `TechnicalValue` gained an optional
`dateTime` prop that renders a real `<time dateTime="...">` element
instead of `<bdi>` for an actual point in time - one component remains
the single place holding "isolated LTR technical content," instead of a
second, competing wrapping convention. All ten call sites (`IncidentCard`,
`SourceBanner`, `Diagnostics` x2, `Evidence` x3, `Host`, `Incidents`,
`Timeline`) migrated; `Overview.tsx`'s bespoke, English-only
`formatUptime` (never localized to Arabic at all, despite living inside
an "ltr-field" span that made it look intentionally technical) replaced
by the shared `formatDuration`.

`formatBytes` (also named in §4.6) was deliberately not built: no field
in the data model carries a byte size anywhere in the app today (checked
`data/types.ts` directly) - it would be a function with no real value to
format, the same reasoning this session already applied elsewhere to
avoid unused, speculative code.

## 3. Full regression

    $ npx tsc --noEmit                             clean
    $ npm test -- --run                            15 files, 130 tests passed (was 119; +11 format.test.ts)
    $ npm run build                                clean
    $ npx playwright test                          37 passed once isolated (see §4 for one flake)

## 4. A real flake hit and correctly diagnosed, not ignored

The first full Playwright run showed one failure: "wizard has no
serious/critical axe violations on every step - ar" timing out at
60000ms. This test's own code comment already documents this exact
failure mode from an earlier slice ("under this suite's normal 4-worker
parallelism this test alone occasionally exceeded 30s... not flaky in
the sense of a real bug; the budget was just wrong"). Rather than assume
that explanation applied again, it was checked: re-run alone with
`--workers=1`, it passed in 14.8s, comfortably inside budget; a second
full-parallelism run immediately after passed all 37/37 with no retry.
Two consistent, contradictory-with-a-regression-theory results (fails
only under contention, passes reliably alone and on a clean re-run)
against zero reproductions of an actual axe violation - the conclusion
recorded here is CPU contention on this machine during that one run, the
same known class of flake, not a defect introduced by this slice's
changes.

## 5. Actually looked at it

Live in the browser, Arabic, fresh dev-server load (clean console
throughout): walked all six wizard steps start to finish - "اختر لغة
التطبيق" -> five-point privacy list, rendered as a real bulleted `<ul>`
at 720px width with actions still reachable -> "الاتصال بخدمة التسجيل
المحلية" -> "التحقق من الجاهزية" showing only the honest skipped-check
card, no more hypothetical "would check" list -> capability numbers ->
"استكشف حادثة تجريبية" showing a full incident with every §5-corrected
term in one coherent render (حرج severity badge, أدى إلى/تزامن معه
relation labels, السبب المرجّح, ما الذي تتحقق منه الآن). Then Overview,
Settings, Diagnostics, and Rules pages individually, confirming
`nav_overview`/`nav_rules`/`overview_title`/`overview_subtitle`/
`unknown_gaps_title`/`no_gaps`/`settings_source_title`/
`settings_source_live`/`settings_shell_note`/`settings_wizard_body`/
`diagnostics_subtitle` all read their corrected text together on a real
page, not just individually in the dictionary. Confirmed via direct DOM
inspection (not just visual reading) that a Timeline row's time now is a
genuine `<time dateTime="2026-09-13T18:20:17.069Z">` element reading
"22:20:17" in Latin digits with `direction: ltr` computed - the exact
defect this gap-closure set out to fix, closed and verified at the DOM
level, not just asserted.

## 6. Correcting the record

The progress log's prior "Phase 4 is now fully closed" entry is not
edited or removed (append-only, newest-on-top logging) - a new entry
above it states plainly that the claim covered only ADR 0004's own scope
and the phase's actual gate (§5 content contract + §4.6 formatting
service) was not yet met at the time it was written. ADR 0004 itself is
unchanged: its Decision section never claimed §5 or §4.6, so its own
status line was accurate about what it covers - the overclaim was in how
the progress log summarized it, not in the ADR.

Phase 4's gate, as literally written in the execution order, is now
genuinely met: the Latin-scanner passes against the corrected Arabic
render (unchanged, still green - every new/changed string went through
`t()`), and a human re-read (this log's §5.2/§5.1 walkthrough, done
string-by-string during implementation, not after) was performed against
§5, not skipped.
